    "hypothesis": "Keeping a sieve through sqrt(maximum) while a separate bitwise prepass handles divisors 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, and 13 may reduce repeated divisor work across the full candidate set; the sieve then checks only larger prime factors.",
    "notes": "The candidate retains generic fragment widths and checked arithmetic, classifies every pair, preserves duplicates, and sorts results. Performance and correctness should be evaluated by the controller; no measurements are claimed.",
